{"step_index":50,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:03:46Z","input_tokens":22597,"cache_read_tokens":97271,"output_tokens":1022,"thinking":"The old file's action names show \"动作\" where the new one shows \"Action\", which I think comes from the locale the original was built in, since the animated matrices match and the names are cosmetic. Not a defect, but worth noting. Now I'm looking at the material node trees, which have changed, and the list of affected materials, starting with V5_Flag_4 and Roof, needs a closer look.\n\nThe material node trees have changed across many materials, V5_Flag_4, Roof, Barrier, SkyDome, LightStrip, Brake150, and the clay materials like CLAY_Car. That's more than the grass and asphalt I expected to differ, so I suspect the same locale issue is at play, with node names translated into Chinese in the old file. I'll diff by node type and input values, ignoring the node names.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"@'\nimport json\nS = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\16b5f3cb-4bce-43d1-a09a-ebf98bd665b7\\scratch\"\nfor a,b in ((\"ref/old_anim_1117.json\",\"run_r1/v5_stage_anim.json\"),(\"ref/old_clay_1117.json\",\"run_r1/v5_stage_anim_clay.json\")):\n    A=json.load(open(S+\"/\"+a,encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"materials\"]; B=json.load(open(S+\"/\"+b,encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"materials\"]\n    for m in sorted(set(A)&set(B)):\n        na=A[m].get(\"nodes\"); nb=B[m].get(\"nodes\")\n        if na==nb and A[m].get(\"links\")==B[m].get(\"links\"): continue\n        ta=sorted((n[0],json.dumps(n[2])) for n in na or []); tb=sorted((n[0],json.dumps(n[2])) for n in nb or [])\n        print(\"==\",m, \"names:\", [n[1] for n in na or []], \"->\", [n[1] for n in nb or []])\n        if ta!=tb:\n            sa=set(ta); sb=set(tb)\n            for x in sorted(sa-sb): print(\"   OLD only:\", x[0], x[1][:300])\n            for x in sorted(sb-sa): print(\"   NEW only:\", x[0], x[1][:300])\n        else:\n            print(\"   same node types+values (names/links only)\")\n            la=A[m][\"links\"]; lb=B[m][\"links\"]; print(\"   links old\",len(la),\"new\",len(lb))\n'@ | python - 2>&1 | Select-Object -Skip 21","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolSummary":"Diff material node trees"}}]}
